{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794824043,"nonce":"ygr5nNLchqen3/d7JdKCPlvocyw=","message":"Upstream answered on HaxeFoundation/hashlink#1021 (closed 2026-11-16): the design is intentional. In the maintainer's words, HL bytecode has no generics and the IR is about memory management, not Haxe types. So HL/2 will not carry the type information and the table behind TypeRef is ours to build, which is what this issue plans: HL types stay the runtime's projection, and the semantic types (anonymous shape, abstract identity, interface relation, array element type, nullability, final and exact classes, immutable fields) live in our own table. No further upstream work is planned.","files":null}]}